<del></del></span> Best Discipline Priest Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>You don't have to worry too much about whether a trinket is passive or active, since the active ones are only available at a lower item level.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=103987/yulons-bite">
<img alt="Yu'lon's Bite" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_jadeserpentpet.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Yu'lon's Bite</span></a> <i>(Timeless Coins)</i> - A great Intellect /<wbr/> Crit stat stick. This will beat out most of your Celestial alternatives so lock it in until you get raid items.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102299/prismatic-prison-of-pride">
<img alt="Prismatic Prison of Pride" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_09.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Prismatic Prison of Pride</span></a> <i>(Sha of Pride)</i> - A powerful trinket that replaces typical passive intellect with an interesting secondary stat amplification.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102309/dysmorphic-samophlange-of-discontinuity">
<img alt="Dysmorphic Samophlange of Discontinuity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dysmorphic Samophlange of Discontinuity</span></a> <i>(Siegecrafted Blackfuse)</i> - The raids premier regeneration trinket. While extra mana isn't bad, we usually have better tools to deal with it such that a pure regeneration trinket isn't necessary.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102304/thoks-acid-grooved-tooth">
<img alt="Thok's Acid-Grooved Tooth" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Acid-Grooved Tooth</span></a> <i>(Thok the Bloodthirsty)</i> - The cleave effect does work off of atonement healing, but it will not proc Divine Aegis or Spirit Shell making this quite a poor option for Discipline Priest unless the raid is very stacked.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102294/nazgrims-burnished-insignia">
<img alt="Nazgrim's Burnished Insignia" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_18.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nazgrim's Burnished Insignia</span></a> <i>(General Nazgrim)</i> - Worse for Discipline than most other healing specs, but still competitive with the fairly weak overall trinket choices for the spec.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102293/purified-bindings-of-immerseus">
<img alt="Purified Bindings of Immerseus" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Bindings of Immerseus</span></a> <i>(Immerseus)</i> - We have no clear way to proc the second effect but the amplification itself is reasonably strong.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Discipline Priest</span></h2>With the removal of Raid Finder in Mists of Pandaria Classic, it is possible to earn your Legendary Cloak without ever setting foot into a raid.  This can be done inside Celestial Dungeons now instead.  <br/>
<br/>We can use two of them as Discipline. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102247/jina-kang-kindness-of-chi-ji">
<img alt="Jina-Kang, Kindness of Chi-Ji" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_cranehealer_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jina-Kang, Kindness of Chi-Ji</span></a> is a healing-focused option, and <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102246/xing-ho-breath-of-yulon">
<img alt="Xing-Ho, Breath of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_dragoncaster_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Xing-Ho, Breath of Yu'lon</span></a> is a damage-focused option that adds no healing at all. I'd recommend you use the healing cloak for progression, but both are 100% viable depending on whether you want to bring more damage or more healing to the raid.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c5" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Discipline Priests</span></h2>Most crafted items don't require you to have the profession anymore. We can wear Tailoring items, for example, even if we aren't Tailors. Note that there are some exceptions to this which we'll note below.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-3-crafted-items-expensive-high-level">Phase 3 Crafted Items (Expensive, high level)</h4>
